# Cursor Rules — SauceDemo BDD

## Language & Framework
- TypeScript (strict: false), Playwright, Cucumber BDD
- Use `import` not `require` in .ts files
- All async functions return `Promise<void>` or typed promises

## Locators
- ONLY `[data-test="..."]` selectors
- Never XPath, never CSS classes, never text selectors
- SauceDemo slugifies item names: "Sauce Labs Backpack" → `sauce-labs-backpack`

## Page Objects
- Extend `BasePage` from `src/pages/base.page.ts`
- Locators as getters returning strings: `get myEl() { return '[data-test="my-el"]'; }`
- Methods are async, use `this.click()`, `this.fill()`, `this.getText()` from BasePage

## Step Definitions
- Always type `this: PlaywrightWorld` as first parameter
- Import `PlaywrightWorld` from `../../fixtures/world`
- Use `getUser(role, env)` for credentials — never hardcode
- No `page.waitForTimeout()` — use Playwright auto-waiting

## Cucumber World
- `this.page` — Playwright Page
- `this.config` — EnvConfig (baseUrl, env, locale, viewport, headless, slowMo)
- `this.browser`, `this.context` — managed by hooks, don't recreate

## Tags
- `@smoke` for critical path scenarios
- `@regression` for full coverage
- Feature files get both: `@smoke @regression` at feature level

## File Naming
- Pages: `src/pages/<name>.page.ts`
- Steps: `src/steps/<domain>/<name>.steps.ts`
- Features: `src/features/<domain>/<name>.feature`

## Imports
- Use relative paths (not path aliases) in step/page files
- Path aliases (@pages, @steps, @config, @utils) are for tsconfig only
